Compare or sync .env with a hosting platform's variables (Vercel).

`diff` shows what differs between a local .env and a Vercel environment;
`pull` writes Vercel's readable values into the local file. Vercel has two
kinds of variable: a Config value can be read back, a Secret never can, so
`diff` cannot compare Secrets and `pull` cannot fetch them. Values are
never printed.

Needs a Vercel token in VERCEL_TOKEN (or --token-file) and a project
(--project, VERCEL_PROJECT_ID, or .vercel/project.json from `vercel link`).

A failed Vercel request has its own exit code (10, 11, 13, 15; 14 when
`push` finds a variable changed on Vercel). See the table below.

Usage: evnx platform [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  diff  Show what differs between a local .env and a Vercel environment
  pull  Write Vercel's readable values into the local file
  push  Create and update Vercel variables from the local file
  help  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --no-color
          Disable colored output

  -q, --quiet
          Print nothing on success. Findings, warnings, errors and requested data still print

  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  evnx platform diff --to vercel                         what differs from Vercel's development variables
  evnx platform diff --to vercel --target production   .env.production against production
  evnx platform pull --to vercel --dry-run               what a pull would change, nothing written
  evnx platform pull --to vercel --yes                   write Vercel's readable values, no question

Auth: VERCEL_TOKEN, or --token-file <path>. There is no --token flag.
Project: --project / --team, or VERCEL_PROJECT_ID / VERCEL_ORG_ID, or .vercel/project.json.
Config variables can be read back; Secrets cannot, so they are compared by presence only
and never pulled. Values are never printed.

Exit codes:
  0  Ran, nothing to report
  1  Ran, and found something: findings, problems, a difference, not in sync
  2  Could not run: usage, config, I/O, or refused before any change
  4  Declined: answered no, or a confirmation was needed with no terminal and no --yes
  10  Not signed in, or the token was rejected
  11  Forbidden, or the email is not verified
  13  Server unreachable, not an evnx server, or TLS roots unusable
  14  Conflict, or locked
  15  Server error, or rate limited
  141  Output closed early (broken pipe)

Full guide: https://docs.evnx.dev/cli/commands/platform
